ypeFont", "line": 91, "var": "faceA", "code": "FT_New_Memory_Face(engineA->lib, (FT_Byte *)fontBufA->getCString(), fontBufA->getLength(), fontNum, &faceA)", "note": "The embedded TrueType font from the PDF is passed to FreeType\'s FT_New_Memory_Face, which triggers font table loading including the GPOS table."},\n{"step": 8, "file": "src/sfnt/sfobjs.c", "function": "sfnt_load_face", "line": 1034, "var": "face", "code": "LOAD_(gpos);", "note": "During face loading, the GPOS table is loaded via tt_face_load_gpos, which reads the GPOS table header and feature list."},\n{"step": 9, "file": "src/sfnt/ttgpos.c", "function": "tt_face_load_gpos", "line": 349, "var": "table_size", "code": "if (table_size < 4) { error = FT_THROW(Table_Missing); goto Exit; }", "note": "The GPOS table size check only rejects tables smaller than 4 bytes. A 4-byte GPOS table passes this check, but the GPOS header is actually 10 bytes, so subsequent reads at offsets 6+ are out of bounds."},\n{"step": 10, "file": "src/sfnt/ttgpos.c", "function": "tt_face_load_gpos", "line": 356, "var": "face->gpos_table", "code": "FT_FRAME_EXTRACT(table_size, face->gpos_table)", "note": "The 4-byte GPOS table is extracted into a heap buffer of exactly 4 bytes. face->gpos_table points to this 4-byte heap allocation."},\n{"step": 11, "file": "src/sfnt/ttgpos.c", "function": "tt_face_load_gpos", "line": 363, "var": "feature_list", "code": "FT_Byte* feature_list = face->gpos_table + FT_PEEK_USHORT(face->gpos_table + 6);", "note": "FT_PEEK_USHORT(face->gpos_table + 6) reads 2 bytes at offset 6 from a 4-byte heap buffer, causing a heap-buffer-overflow READ. The featureListOffset value read from out-of-bounds memory is then added to gpos_table to compute feature_list, which points far beyond the 4-byte buffer."},\n{"step": 12, "file": "src/sfnt/ttgpos.c", "function": "tt_face_load_gpos", "line": 364, "var": "feature_count", "code": "FT_UInt16 feature_count = FT_PEEK_USHORT(feature_list);", "note": "FT_PEEK_USHORT(feature_list) reads 2 bytes from feature_list, which points beyond the 4-byte GPOS table heap buffer, causing another heap-buffer-overflow READ. The value read is treated as the feature count for the loop."},\n{"step": 13, "file": "src/sfnt/ttgpos.c", "function": "tt_face_load_gpos", "line": 365, "var": "feature_records", "code": "FT_Byte* feature_records = feature_list + 2;", "note": "feature_records is computed as feature_list + 2, still pointing beyond the heap buffer."},\n{"step": 14, "file": "src/sfnt/ttgpos.c", "function": "tt_face_load_gpos", "line": 369, "var": "feature_tag", "code": "FT_ULong feature_tag = FT_PEEK_ULONG(feature_records);", "note": "FT_PEEK_ULONG(feature_records) reads 4 bytes from feature_records, which is beyond the 4-byte GPOS table heap buffer, causing a heap-buffer-overflow READ of size 4. The compiler may combine this with the adjacent 2-byte reads into a single 8-byte read, matching the ASAN \'READ of size 8\' report."},\n{"step": 15, "file": "src/sfnt/ttgpos.c", "function": "tt_face_load_gpos", "line": 371, "var": "feature_tag", "code": "if (feature_tag == TTAG_kern) { face->gpos_kerning_available = TRUE; break; }", "note": "The out-of-bounds read value is compared against the \'kern\' tag. If the garbage bytes happen to match, gpos_kerning_available is set, but the crash has already occurred from the out-of-bounds read."}]', task_completed=None, outputs={}, thought='', action=<ActionType.FINISH: 'finish'>)
